Shell builtin commands
cd DIR - change current dir to DIR - if DIR not supplied the value of the HOME shell variable is used as DIR

If cd uses a non-empty directory name from CDPATH, or if - is the first argument, and the directory change is
successful, cd writes the absolute pathname of the new working directory to the standard output.

If the directory change is successful, cd sets the value of the PWD environment variable to the new directory name, and
sets the OLDPWD environment variable to the value of the current working directory before the change.

The return value is true if the directory was successfully changed; false otherwise.

