Executor shld
- walk the command tree and run it
- Input - AST (command structure) from parser
- Output - side effects (forks, exec, pipes, redirections, builtins)
- Steps 
    a) for a pipeline
    - create N pipes
    - For each command
        - fork()
        - In child - dup2() appropriate pipe ends, apply redirections then execve()
        In parent - close used pipe ends, waitpid()
    
    b) for heredocs
    - collect heredoc input during preprocessing (before children are forked)
    - store heredoc input in a temp file or pipe
    - During execution, connect that file/pipe to the command's stdin

- handle && / || logic (short-circuiting)
- handle builtins (cd, export, exit) directly in parent (no fork, unless in a pipeline)

